Define the complete semantic contract for component `control_unit` before its VHDL is written. Return Markdown only. This contract will be normative for the VHDL implementation, Cocotb tests, and dependent components. Do not infer or mention implementation internals. State timing, reset behavior (or `none`), all input/output semantics, every opcode/selector encoding when applicable, and boundary behavior. Use exactly these level-2 headings: `## Timing`, `## Reset`, `## Behavior`, `## Operations`, `## Edge cases`, and `## Test strategy`. `## Operations` may say `none` only when there is no encoded selector.

The test strategy is normative and must be an executable evidence plan, not generic coverage advice. For each public behavior that selects, indexes, routes, packs, slices, extends, decodes, or transforms data: identify control classes, state the causal input-to-output relation, require distinguishable source values where a wrong selection could otherwise pass, and vary one semantic factor at a time. Do not mention implementation internals.

Responsibility: Decode opcode, funct3, and funct7 fields to produce all control signals: ALU operation selector, ALU source mux select, memory read/write enable, memory width, register write enable, memory-to-register select, branch/jump/jump-register enables, and immediate type selector.
Fixed decomposition (approved architecture): `control_unit` has no generated dependencies.
Public interface:
```vhdl
entity control_unit is
    port(
        opcode : in std_logic_vector(6 downto 0);
        funct3 : in std_logic_vector(2 downto 0);
        funct7 : in std_logic_vector(6 downto 0);
        alu_op : out std_logic_vector(3 downto 0);
        alu_src : out std_logic;
        mem_read : out std_logic;
        mem_write : out std_logic;
        mem_width : out std_logic_vector(1 downto 0);
        mem_to_reg : out std_logic;
        reg_write : out std_logic;
        branch : out std_logic;
        jump : out std_logic;
        jump_reg : out std_logic;
        imm_sel : out std_logic_vector(2 downto 0)
    );
end control_unit;
```

